  "caveats": [
    "The determinism floor is EXACTLY zero: the repeat arm reproduced its twin bit for bit across a full checkpoint reload, both arms genuinely rendered (sampler 14.9 s and 19.7 s, neither flagged as a cache hit). A fixed-input first-step forward is bit-deterministic on this box.",
    "That makes the entry's '10x floor' test degenerate -- with a floor of zero any non-zero value passes it, so that clause discriminated nothing here. It did not matter: the measured values are percent-scale, not noise-scale.",
    "This is a first-step forward, not a render. It says the velocity differs; it says nothing about how that difference propagates over a full schedule, and nothing about whether anyone could see it. A perceptual claim would need its own blind session under docs/eval_comparison.md section 3.",
    "The entry's pre-registered prediction was S under 1% on both checkpoints. Measured: 5.6% to 9.4%. The prediction was wrong by roughly an order of magnitude and is recorded as wrong rather than quietly dropped.",
    "The entry's profile clause carries no threshold, so the grader implements the weakest testable reading: deepest block at least twice block 0. The measured profile is not a monotone opening -- q error peaks at block 36 and falls back at 49 on both checkpoints. The verdict did not turn on it."
  ]
